{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1565074-can-mages-use-spheres-outside-their-watchtower-canonically","id":1565074,"title":"can mages use spheres outside their watchtower canonically","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-11-01T10:13:15-08:00","id":1565074,"title":"can mages use spheres outside their watchtower canonically","content":"could a obrimos use fate or mind, or a acanthus use death or matter?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27683-bernese","name":"Bernese","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-11-01T11:02:53-08:00","id":1565075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bernese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1565074-can-mages-use-spheres-outside-their-watchtower-canonically#post1565074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">could a obrimos use fate or mind, or a acanthus use death or matter?</div> </div> </div> </div>A mage can learn Any Arcana, the Path only set the maximum learnable level without the need of a teacher (see page 84)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-11-01T14:47:02-08:00","id":1565076,"title":"","content":"There are three limitations to a mage learning and using Arcana not Ruled by their Path.<br /> <br /> 1. A mage can study all five degrees of their Ruling Arcana on their own without a teacher, but requires a teacher to learn the fifth degree of other Arcana, and it costs one more experience to learn that fifth degree.<br /> 2. Each Path has an Inferior Arcanum. A mage requires a teacher to learn their Inferior Arcanum to the third degree or higher, and it costs one more experience to do so. A mage's starting Arcanum dots in character generation cannot go to their Inferior Arcanum.<br /> 3. A mage casting a spell outside of their Ruling Arcana which they have not learned as a rote or a praxis must spend one Mana to cast the spell, in addition to any other cost it has.<br /> <br /> That's more or less it. A mage of any Path can become a fifth-degree master in all of the Arcana, even their Inferior Arcanum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-11-02T07:00:41-08:00","id":1565079,"title":"","content":"I think the more interesting question is how many NPC mages learn more than a dot or two in arcana outside of their ruling arcana? BTW, I mean a dot or two per arcana not a dot or two overall although the even more restrictive reading is certainly viable. It is completely up the the GM and players of course but it can be an interesting thought experiment. It makes PCs stand out a little more and potentially makes legacies a bigger deal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28478-madmarcus","name":"Madmarcus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-11-02T08:50:27-08:00","id":1565080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madmarcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1565074-can-mages-use-spheres-outside-their-watchtower-canonically?p=1565079#post1565079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the more interesting question is how many NPC mages learn more than a dot or two in arcana outside of their ruling arcana? BTW, I mean a dot or two per arcana not a dot or two overall although the even more restrictive reading is certainly viable. It is completely up the the GM and players of course but it can be an interesting thought experiment. It makes PCs stand out a little more and potentially makes legacies a bigger deal.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, all NPC I can remember have multiple arcana, even at lower levels, rather than focus on a couple of arcana.<br /> <br /> It makes sense in universe, a broad set of arcana would cover a varied set of situations, if you make them rotes or praxes, that voids the mana cost and the main limitation on usage.<br /> <br /> Unless you prepare a lot, have ample set of skills and merits, and/or a cabal around; diversification seems almost mandatory for low level mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-11-02T11:32:47-08:00","id":1565081,"title":"","content":"I didn't explain myself well. If we take the rules as a simulation of fictional world you are absolutely right.<br /> <br /> The thought experiment is about what if the NPCs aren't quite playing with the same rules. Not a big deal since often GMs don't strictly make their NPCs using the full rules anyway. In this case have NPCs rarely invest in arcana outside of their ruling arcana. A few dots sure but enough that NPC mages taken as a whole are noticeably more predictable and less flexible as individuals. Maybe the assumption is that arcana that aren't ruling arcana are harder to learn but not enough harder to learn to be actually worth costing more for PCs. Or really focus on the idea that the watchtowers (and thus the arcana) are tightly tied to the mage's personality so that most people feel a natural pull towards their ruling arcana beyond the purely mechanical bits in the rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28478-madmarcus","name":"Madmarcus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-11-02T11:42:25-08:00","id":1565082,"title":"","content":"Assuming you attempt to solve all of your problems using magic, of course; and/or by yourself. Cabals exist for a reason. <br /> <br /> And the more you diversify, the less you can do in any one Arcanum anyway. While it's not quite as bad as Ascension's &quot;one dot lets you perceive things&quot;, a mage with three dots split between three Arcana isn't going to be able to do much in the way of using magic to solve their problems, anyway. Having two or three dots in a single Arcanum is nothing to sneeze at; and having no dots in 8 or 9 Arcana isn't all that different from having no dots in 7 Arcana. <br /> <br /> And remember that unlike Ascension, Awakening makes a point to let you do a much as possible using each Arcanum on its own. That translates to a reduced incentive to diversify, since you don't get a much synergistic benefit from using multiple Arcana together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-11-03T14:07:15-08:00","id":1565106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madmarcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1565074-can-mages-use-spheres-outside-their-watchtower-canonically?p=1565081#post1565081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't explain myself well. If we take the rules as a simulation of fictional world you are absolutely right.<br /> <br /> The thought experiment is about what if the NPCs aren't quite playing with the same rules. Not a big deal since often GMs don't strictly make their NPCs using the full rules anyway. In this case have NPCs rarely invest in arcana outside of their ruling arcana. A few dots sure but enough that NPC mages taken as a whole are noticeably more predictable and less flexible as individuals. Maybe the assumption is that arcana that aren't ruling arcana are harder to learn but not enough harder to learn to be actually worth costing more for PCs. Or really focus on the idea that the watchtowers (and thus the arcana) are tightly tied to the mage's personality so that most people feel a natural pull towards their ruling arcana beyond the purely mechanical bits in the rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect NPC write-ups in general probably have a broader range of Arcana developed to higher levels than the typical PC would.<br /> <br /> NPCs aren't really tracking their development by XP, but I think the incentives built in apply similar pressures in character. For four experience points, that each took five beats to create, you can either buy the first dot of a new Arcanum that can only do relatively minor things, or you can buy your fourth or fifth dot in a well-developed Arcanum that lets you do some very powerful things.<br /> <br /> I think the idea that it's a hard inclination created by the Path is a bit iffy, when it's easy enough to account for with the aforementioned point in combination with &quot;no mana cost for improvised spells will make Ruling Arcana use second nature&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-11-03T17:15:43-08:00","id":1565115,"title":"","content":"Personal note, my characters focus almost exclusively in the Ruling Arcana (Path and Legacy-granted). Lack of Mana cost makes easier to just use them over and over; higher ratings in the Arcana I have found more useful than broad expenditures.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}